      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/tufte-css/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve switched my Hugo theme from &lt;a href=&#34;https://themes.gohugo.io/themes/shibui/&#34; class=&#34;sg-ext&#34;&gt;Shibui&lt;/a&gt; to SIGIL, which you&amp;rsquo;re likely looking at now. It looks far nicer, and also comes with way more cool features. For example, check out the Tufte-style footnotes!&lt;sup id=&#34;fnref:1&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#fn:1&#34; class=&#34;footnote-ref&#34; role=&#34;doc-noteref&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; It&amp;rsquo;s kind of hilarious that both of my posts here so far involve footnotes&amp;hellip; in all seriousness, I find this to be quite cool. I&amp;rsquo;m used to having footnotes shoved to the bottom of the page, so this is a nice change of pace. &lt;a href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Tufte&#34; class=&#34;sg-ext&#34;&gt;Tufte&lt;/a&gt; for the win.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
